  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "New: x.SqlParam() and x.SqlIdentifier() -- the two doors a raw string can take into SQL, now discoverable in IntelliSense with no extra using. Sql.Text is deprecated in favour of x.SqlParam() (warning; removed in 2.0). Sql.Identifier is unchanged.\n\nFixes: ToDebug() on SQL Server emitted DECLARE @@p001_x -- a doubled @, which is T-SQL's system-variable prefix, so the script was invalid and could not be pasted into SSMS. Parameter names could contain characters SQL rejects (Sql.Text(\"literal\") produced @p001_\"literal\"). Parameter scopes are now 1-based, so the first command emits @p001_* as the docs have always said -- it was emitting @p000_*.\n\nNOTE: generated parameter NAMES change in this release. They are not API, but if you hardcoded one in AppendRaw or snapshot-tested generated SQL, you will see a diff.\n\nFull notes: https://github.com/purelogictek-inc/DapperPipeline/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md",
